          <button class="viz-btn" onclick="window.print()">Print</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main id="main-content">
    <div class="poster" id="posterRoot" role="document" aria-label="Academic poster: IMF WEO global outlook trends 2024 to 2026">

      <section class="header" aria-label="Poster header">
        <div>
          <h1 class="title">Global Economy in the Shadow of War</h1>
          <div class="subtitle">IMF World Economic Outlook trends (Jul 2024–Apr 2026): persistent mediocrity in a ~3.0–3.3% growth band, with a risk balance consistently tilted to the downside.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="venue">
          <div class="badge">
            <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>IMF–World Bank Annual Meetings · Research Symposium</span>
          </div>
          <div class="meta">
            Prepared from eight WEO editions (updates + main reports)<br>
            Time window: Jul 2024 → Apr 2026
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-label="Key metrics">
        <div class="kpi-row">
          <div class="kpi accent">
            <div class="label">Global growth band (headline)</div>
            <div class="value">3.0–3.3%</div>
          </div>
          <div class="kpi">
            <div class="label">Pre‑pandemic average</div>
            <div class="value">~3.8%</div>
          </div>
          <div class="kpi">
            <div class="label">Editions reviewed</div>
            <div class="value">8</div>
          </div>
          <div class="kpi">
            <div class="label">2025 projection (Jul 2025)</div>
            <div class="value">3.0%</div>
          </div>
          <div class="kpi warning">
            <div class="label">Risk balance</div>
            <div class="value">Downside</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="grid" aria-label="Main content grid">
        <section class="card" aria-label="Growth trajectory">
          <h2>Global Growth Projections: A Narrow Band of Mediocrity</h2>
          <p>Across eight WEO editions, the outlook rarely breaks out of a tight range. The projection path is stable, but stability is not strength: growth remains below the historical ~3.8% average.</p>

          <div class="callout" role="note" aria-label="Persistent risk finding">
            <div class="headline">Tilted to the downside — every edition</div>
            <div class="body">The IMF repeatedly emphasizes that downside risks dominate: trade policy escalation, geopolitical tensions, and inflation persistence raise the probability of growth underperforming an already-low baseline.</div>
          </div>

          <div class="chart-wrap" aria-label="Chart container">
            <canvas id="growthChart" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of IMF global growth projections across WEO editions, showing a tight band around 3.0 to 3.3 percent"></canvas>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-caption">
            <div>
              <span class="pill"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Projection band (3.0–3.3%)</span>
              <span class="pill"><span class="dot warn" aria-hidden="true"></span>Downside risk emphasis</span>
            </div>
            <div style="text-align:right;">Note: Several editions provide qualitative wording (“slowing”, “renewed pressure”). These are encoded as missing points, with the band highlighted.</div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mini-grid" aria-label="Right column">
          <section class="card" aria-label="Dominant downside risks">
            <h2>Dominant Downside Risks</h2>
            <p>Recurring threats in the IMF narrative: policy shocks, conflict, valuation corrections, and sticky services inflation.</p>
            <div class="list" role="list">
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Trade policy escalation</div>
                  <div class="desc">Tariffs and retaliation (especially from 2025 onward) distort activity via front‑loading, then weigh on investment and trade volumes.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Geopolitical fractures</div>
                  <div class="desc">Middle East conflict and broader security tensions raise energy, shipping, and risk‑premium channels.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Technology re‑evaluation</div>
                  <div class="desc">AI‑linked optimism could correct—tightening financial conditions through wealth and investment channels.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Persistent services inflation (US)</div>
                  <div class="desc">A slower return to target delays easing relative to peers, reinforcing global rate differentials and volatility.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="card" aria-label="Inflation outlook">
            <h2>Inflation Outlook and Monetary Policy</h2>
            <p>Disinflation supports a “policy pivot” toward easing, but the path is uneven; renewed inflation pressure appears by Apr 2026 amid defense spending and disruptions.</p>
            <div class="timeline" aria-label="Inflation narrative timeline">
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Late 2024</div>
                <div class="what"><b>Policy pivot</b> begins as inflation declines; emphasis on careful sequencing.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">2025</div>
                <div class="what">Disinflation continues, but <b>services inflation</b> slows progress in the US.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Apr 2026</div>
                <div class="what"><b>Renewed pressure</b> risks re‑accelerating prices via supply disruption and fiscal‑defense trade‑offs.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="card" aria-label="Policy evolution">
            <h2>Evolving Policy Priorities</h2>
            <p>The narrative spine: recommendations evolve from safeguarding disinflation → rebuilding buffers → predictable frameworks → defense‑spending trade‑offs.</p>
            <div class="timeline" aria-label="Policy timeline">
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Mid‑2024</div>
                <div class="what">Manage disinflation; calibrate easing without reigniting inflation.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Late‑2024</div>
                <div class="what">Ensure <b>fiscal sustainability</b> as monetary policy pivots.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Early‑2025</div>
                <div class="what">Rebuild <b>fiscal buffers</b>; address demographic and gender gaps.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Mid/Late‑2025</div>
                <div class="what">Restore confidence amid tariff uncertainty; strengthen frameworks and industrial policy discipline.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="t-row">
                <div class="when">Early‑2026</div>
                <div class="what"><b>Agile policy</b>: manage defense‑spending trade‑offs while laying foundations for recovery.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="card" aria-label="Special themes">
            <h2>Special Themes Across WEO Editions</h2>
            <p>Deep‑dive chapters broaden from stabilization to inclusive, sustainable growth constraints.</p>
            <div class="list" role="list">
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true" style="background:var(--accent);"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Industrial policy: effectiveness & fiscal cost</div>
                  <div class="desc">Evidence and trade‑offs of targeted support under tighter fiscal space.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true" style="background:var(--accent);"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Social acceptability of structural reforms</div>
                  <div class="desc">Implementation constraints matter for growth‑enhancing reforms.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="risk-item" role="listitem">
                <div class="bullet" aria-hidden="true" style="background:var(--accent);"></div>
                <div>
                  <div class="title">Demographics, gender, and migration</div>
                  <div class="desc">Labor supply, participation, and skill alignment as medium‑term growth levers.</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </section>
      </section>

      <section class="footer" aria-label="Footer">
        <div class="source-box">
          Sources: IMF World Economic Outlook (WEO) editions from Jul 2024 through Apr 2026 (as summarized in provided brief). Chart encodes headline global growth projections when numeric values are given.
        </div>
        <div class="source-box" style="text-align:right;">
          Poster size: A0 portrait · Render target: 4961×7016 px
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <script>
    function toggleMenu() {
      var el = document.getElementById('vizMenuDropdown');
      if (!el) return;
      el.classList.toggle('open');
    }

    function setTheme(mode) {
      var root = document.documentElement;
      root.classList.remove('theme-light', 'theme-dark');
      root.classList.add(mode === 'dark' ? 'theme-dark' : 'theme-light');
      localStorage.setItem('viz-theme', mode);
      // Repaint charts to match theme colors
      initCharts();
    }

    (function initTheme() {
      var saved = localStorage.getItem('viz-theme');
      if (saved === 'dark' || saved === 'light') {
        setTheme(saved);
      } else {
        // Default to light for print/poster readability
        setTheme('light');
      }
    })();

    async function downloadImage() {
      var node = document.getElementById('posterRoot');
      if (!node) return;
      try {
        var dataUrl = await htmlToImage.toPng(node, {
          cacheBust: true,
          pixelRatio: 1
        });
        var link = document.createElement('a');
        link.download = 'imf-weo-a0-poster.png';
        link.href = dataUrl;
        link.click();
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('PNG export failed', e);
        alert('PNG export failed. See console for details.');
      }
    }

    function getCssVar(name) {
      return getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(name).trim();
    }

    var ChartManager = {
      charts: new Map(),
      safeInit: function(canvasId, config) {
        if (typeof Chart === 'undefined') { console.error('Chart.js not loaded'); return null; }
        try {
          if (this.charts.has(canvasId)) {
            this.charts.get(canvasId).destroy();
            this.charts.delete(canvasId);
          }
          var canvas = document.getElementById(canvasId);
          if (!canvas) { console.error('Canvas element not found: ' + canvasId); return null; }
          if (canvas.chart) {
            canvas.chart.destroy();
            delete canvas.chart;
          }
          canvas.setAttribute('role', 'img');
          if (!canvas.getAttribute('aria-label')) {
            canvas.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Chart');
          }
          var chart = new Chart(canvas, config);
          canvas.chart = chart;
          this.charts.set(canvasId, chart);
          return chart;
        } catch (e) {
          console.error('Chart init failed for ' + canvasId, e);
          return null;
        }
      }
    };

    function initCharts() {
      if (typeof Chart === 'undefined') { console.error('Chart.js not loaded'); return; }

      var accent = getCssVar('--accent') || '#002244';
      var warning = getCssVar('--warning') || '#d97706';
      var text = getCssVar('--text') || '#0B1220';
      var textSecondary = getCssVar('--text-secondary') || '#4B5563';
      var grid = 'rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.10)';

      // Data: numeric points only; qualitative editions omitted.
      var labels = [
        'Jul 2024\nUpdate',
        'Oct 2024\nWEO',
        'Jan 2025\nUpdate',
        'Apr 2025\nWEO',
        'Jul 2025\nUpdate',
        'Oct 2025\nWEO',
        'Jan 2026\nUpdate',
        'Apr 2026\nWEO'
      ];

      // Global growth projection for the "next year" as commonly highlighted:
      // - For 2024 mid-year editions, show 2025.
      // - For Jan 2025, show 2025.
      // - For Jul 2025, show 2025.
      // - For Jan 2026, show 2026.
      // Missing where brief is qualitative.
      var series = [3.3, 3.3, 3.3, null, 3.0, null, 3.2, null];

      // Band shading: 3.0 to 3.3
      var bandTop = labels.map(function(){ return 3.3; });
      var bandBottom = labels.map(function(){ return 3.0; });

      ChartManager.safeInit('growthChart', {
        type: 'line',
        data: {
          labels: labels,
          datasets: [
            {
              label: 'Projection band (3.0–3.3%)',
              data: bandTop,
              borderColor: 'transparent',
              backgroundColor: 'rgba(217,119,6,0.00)',
              pointRadius: 0,
              tension: 0,
              fill: false
            },
            {
              label: 'Band fill',
              data: bandBottom,
              borderColor: 'transparent',
              backgroundColor: 'rgba(11,79,138,0.12)',
              pointRadius: 0,
              tension: 0,
              fill: {
                target: '-1'
              }
            },
            {
              label: 'Headline global growth (numeric editions)',
              data: series,
              borderColor: accent,
              backgroundColor: accent,
              pointBackgroundColor: accent,
              pointBorderColor: '#ffffff',
              pointBorderWidth: 3,
              pointRadius: 8,
              spanGaps: false,
              tension: 0.18
            }
          ]
        },
        options: {
          responsive: true,
          maintainAspectRatio: false,
          plugins: {
            tooltip: { enabled: true },
            legend: {
              display: true,
              labels: {
                color: textSecondary,
                boxWidth: 18,
                boxHeight: 10,
                padding: 18,
                font: { size: 20, family: 'Inter' }
              }
            },
            title: {
              display: true,
              text: 'Global growth projections across WEO editions (selected headline series)'
            }
          },
          scales: {
            y: {
              min: 2.7,
              max: 3.6,
              ticks: {
                color: textSecondary,
                callback: function(v){ return v.toFixed(1) + '%'; },
                font: { size: 20 }
              },
              grid: { color: grid },
              title: { display: true, text: 'Growth rate', color: textSecondary, font: { size: 20 } }
            },
            x: {
              ticks: {
                color: textSecondary,
                font: { size: 18 },
                maxRotation: 0,
                minRotation: 0
              },
              grid: { display: false }
            }
          }
        }
      });
    }

    // Close menu on outside click
    document.addEventListener('click', function(e) {
      var dd = document.getElementById('vizMenuDropdown');
      var toggle = document.querySelector('.viz-menu-toggle');
      if (!dd || !toggle) return;
      if (!dd.contains(e.target) && !toggle.contains(e.target)) {
        dd.classList.remove('open');
      }
    });

    // Init once DOM is ready
    window.addEventListener('load', function(){
      initCharts();
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
HTML"}
